\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces The $\ensuremath  {d_{L}}\xspace  $--$\iota $ bimodality in the GW170817 flat-in-redshift posterior. Left: joint $(\ensuremath  {d_{L}}\xspace  ,\iota )$ posterior from the unrestricted $\ensuremath  {d_{L}}\xspace  \in [10,75]\,\rm  Mpc$ run (Mode-B-anchored heterodyne reference), with the prior-restricted Mode-A and Mode-B contours overlaid. Right: per-mode \ensuremath  {H_{0}}\xspace  \ marginals as weighted step-histograms. The Planck $\Lambda $CDM and SH0ES distance-ladder bands are shown for context; this work is itself a GW170817 reanalysis, so the LVK GW170817 band is uninformative here and is not included.}}{8}{figure.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:bimodality}{{5}{8}{The $\dL $--$\iota $ bimodality in the GW170817 flat-in-redshift posterior. Left: joint $(\dL ,\iota )$ posterior from the unrestricted $\dL \in [10,75]\,\rm Mpc$ run (Mode-B-anchored heterodyne reference), with the prior-restricted Mode-A and Mode-B contours overlaid. Right: per-mode \hzero \ marginals as weighted step-histograms. The Planck $\Lambda $CDM and SH0ES distance-ladder bands are shown for context; this work is itself a GW170817 reanalysis, so the LVK GW170817 band is uninformative here and is not included}{figure.5}{}}
